  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nWhen a user calls [`requestRedeem()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/main/src/core/MonetrixVault.sol#L183-L196), their USDM is transferred to the vault and [`addObligation()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/main/src/core/RedeemEscrow.sol#L41-L44) increments `totalOwed` in RedeemEscrow. The operator later calls `fundRedemptions` to move the matching USDC into the escrow. When the user eventually calls [`claimRedeem()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/main/src/core/MonetrixVault.sol#L198-L213), the vault calls [`payOut()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/main/src/core/RedeemEscrow.sol#L47-L53) which does `usdc.safeTransfer(recipient, amount)`.\n\nCircle (the USDC issuer) can blacklist any address at any time, including in response to legal orders or theft. If the redeeming user is blacklisted between `requestRedeem` and `claimRedeem`, the `safeTransfer` reverts because USDC enforces a blacklist check on every transfer. There is nothing in the protocol that handles this revert.\n\nThe consequences are permanent:\n\n- `payOut` is the only function that reduces `totalOwed`. With a blacklisted recipient, every call to `payOut` reverts and `totalOwed` can never decrease for that obligation.\n- [`reclaimTo`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/main/src/core/RedeemEscrow.sol#L59-L65) enforces `bal >= amount + totalOwed`. As long as the stuck obligation remains in `totalOwed`, the operator cannot reclaim the corresponding USDC.\n- The user's USDM is sitting in the vault (transferred there at `requestRedeem`) and can never be burned or returned -- there is no refund path.\n- There is no admin or governance function in RedeemEscrow or the vault that can clear a stuck obligation or redirect a payment to an alternative address.\n\n**Accounting impact.** The stuck USDC stays in RedeemEscrow and is still counted as backing by [`totalBackingSigned()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/main/src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol#L117-L135). The corresponding USDM is still in `usdm.totalSupply()` (never burned). So `surplus()` is not distorted -- the accounting stays balanced, just with permanently frozen funds.\n\n---\n\n## Mitigation\n\nThe cleanest fix is to allow the redemption owner to specify an alternative recipient in `claimRedeem`. Since the ownership check already ensures only `req.owner` can call it, they can redirect the USDC to any non-blacklisted address they control. This requires no governance intervention and keeps the existing access control intact.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```\nforge test --match-path \"test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol\" -vvv\n```\n\n```solidity\n// test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol\n\nfunction test_submissionValidity() public {\n    // User deposits and requests redemption. USDM moves to vault, obligation recorded.\n    _deposit(user1, 1_000e6);\n    uint256 requestId = _requestRedeem(user1, 1_000e6);\n\n    // Operator funds the escrow so the USDC is ready for the user to claim.\n    vm.prank(operator);\n    vault.fundRedemptions(0);\n\n    // Cooldown passes. Before the user claims, Circle blacklists their address.\n    vm.warp(block.timestamp + 3 days + 1);\n    vm.mockCallRevert(\n        address(usdc),\n        abi.encodeWithSelector(bytes4(keccak256(\"transfer(address,uint256)\")), user1, 1_000e6),\n        abi.encodeWithSignature(\"Error(string)\", \"Blacklistable: account is blacklisted\")\n    );\n\n    // claimRedeem is permanently bricked for this user.\n    vm.prank(user1);\n    vm.expectRevert(\"Blacklistable: account is blacklisted\");\n    vault.claimRedeem(requestId);\n\n    // The request, the obligation, and the USDC are all permanently stuck.\n    // totalOwed can only decrease via a successful payOut, which always reverts.\n    assertEq(redeemEscrow.totalOwed(), 1_000e6, \"Obligation permanently stuck\");\n    assertEq(usdc.balanceOf(address(redeemEscrow)), 1_000e6, \"USDC permanently locked\");\n\n    // reclaimTo enforces bal >= amount + totalOwed, so the USDC cannot be\n    // reclaimed by the operator either.\n    vm.prank(operator);\n    vm.expectRevert(\"RedeemEscrow: would underfund obligations\");\n    vault.reclaimFromRedeemEscrow(1e6);\n}\n```",
